<font color=white><A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=2132&lastnode_id=175">Tower of Frozen Shadow wrap up</a> (0 Replies)</font></td>
<td align=right bgcolor=#333333>
<nowrap><font color=white>Posted by <A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=1313&lastnode_id=175">Kartane</a> on 2001-08-11 21:07:46</font></nowrap></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan=2>I would like to start off by thanking everyone who showed for the raid. We began with three full groups, which turned into two groups as the hours wore on.  Though we had to contend within LD running rampant, we managed to stick together and made it through the entire tower without a single casualty. I would also like to say that I was very proud of the Horde as we worked our way through the tower.  Orders were followed.  Bickering was absent.  And we all worked together to obtain some nice items for our members.  <br>
<br>
Khormik recieved the Student's Homework.  Vanc won the roll on the Sparkling Soul Necklace.  Boilybut now has a Frost Covered Tome.  Boily seems to be enjoying the brightly colored pictures inside his new book all ready.  Sartassa won a Ceremonial Wedding Sword.  We're not sure what it's for, but it looks terribly nice.  Razorr is now sporting a Talisman of Vhal'Sera.  And little Gnadira snatched up Tserrina's Symbol.  And finally, the terribly lucky Nlain, now has his very own Harnessed Soul Gem.  I'm sure we all know how handy those harnessed souls are.<br>
<br>
The platinum gathered from the kills totalled around 400.  This money was donated to the treasury for the costs that go into raids and other guild functions.  <br>
<br>
Thanks again to everyone, especially to those who were able to stick it out through the entire 9 hours. It was good to be hunting with so many of my family, and after so many hours of work and waiting, we finally got to give that girl a real pounding.  Good work, brothers and sisters!  I am anxious to stalk greater and more challenging prey with each of you again. <br>
<br>
RARRRRR HORDE!<br>
<br>
K  <br>
<br>
<br>
<br>
<br>
<br>
