<font color=white><A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=2117&lastnode_id=175">Tank yoo from Scarlet Underground</a> (0 Replies)</font></td>
<td align=right bgcolor=#333333>
<nowrap><font color=white>Posted by <A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=184&lastnode_id=175">root</a> on 2001-08-05 11:12:14</font></nowrap></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan=2>Me gots dis message from Scarlet Underground last week and me fergot to post it.  Dey was much happy with da Bloodhorde!<br>
<br>
--------<br>
<br>
RRRAAARRRR!  Hail to the Horde!<br>
<br>
    I wanted to drop a line to thank all of you who came and helped make the raid on Hate a success!  Everyone I talked to in our guild had only good things to say about y'all.  I would like to personally thank you for your patience at the start when things were a bit disorganized.  While things got off to a slow start as we (I) learned the zone pathing, we came together as a team as the day went on, and finished the last third of Hate with only ~24 people.  As Kementari said, it seemed like things ran smoother with the smaller (both in terms of numbers and average girth :^) post-exodus group.  I suspect we could clear the first floor again in half the time with fewer people next time around.<br>
<br>
    Anyway, congratulations on the loot and honor you earned!  I hope you enjoyed yourselves, and also hope that we fight together again soon!  Feel free to call on me/us if you are organizing something and could use a few more strong arms to help.  I've always had good experiences grouping with members of the Horde.<br>
<br>
-- Kitzu, raid leader of Scarlet Underground<br>
<br>
